Ok, i think i found the issue.
In the reverseTransform function, we call that
            $dateTime = new \DateTime(sprintf('@%s', $timestamp), new \DateTimeZone($this->outputTimezone));

But we set a timestamp in the constructor, so, the timezone is ignore (as say php documentation).
If we just add 
            $dateTime->setTimezone(new \DateTimeZone($this->outputTimezone));
after the construction of the datetime, it's work well.

the new code should be 

```
$dateTime = new \DateTime(sprintf('@%s', $timestamp));
$dateTime->setTimeZone(new \DateTimeZone($this->outputTimezone));
```
